  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Rio-favela 1985-onward block-party street-music built on the Tamborzão two-bar Brazilian-funk-percussion pattern with Miami-bass / electro-funk roots imported via 1980s American-vinyl-records trade. The genre evolved through four phases: melô-rap early-period (1985-1995, English-language samples over Volt-mix Atomic-Dog DNA), funk-melody and funk-consciente mid-period (1995-2005, Portuguese-language MC vocals layered over 808-kick patterns), proibidão hardcore underground (2000s-onward, drug-trafficking-themed-lyrics often banned from mainstream airwaves), and bregafunk-and-funk-150bpm modern-period (2010s-onward, accelerated-tempo Rio-and-Recife regional variants).",
